Package: rk3588-codec-udev
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: ffmpeg, gnome-remote-desktop
Description: unprivileged RK3588 video codec and RGA device access
 Installs a udev rule granting the video group read/write access to the Rockchip
 MPP codec device, RGA accelerator, and DMA heaps. DMA-heap access is required
 for RKMPP frame and stream allocation.
 .
 Group access only: the shipped rule sets GROUP="video", MODE="0660" and nothing
 else. It does NOT tag the nodes for the active local seat, so a logged-in user
 who is not in "video" gets no access -- add them with usermod -aG video. The
 previous description claimed a seat grant, and the package depended on acl, but
 no setfacl or TAG+="uaccess" was ever present here; the seat/ACL mechanism lives
 in the separate gnome-remote-desktop-gdm-hwenc rule.
